From: notrealOS <53965041+notrealdotmp4@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: simple: agc: Compensate the exposure target for AWB gains

With all AWB gains >= 1.0 the image is brightened after the raw histogram
was measured, so bright scenes came out overexposed.
---
--- a/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/agc.cpp	2026-10-10 16:36:04.726219273 +0200
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/agc.cpp	2026-10-10 16:36:04.736593368 +0200
@@ -70,7 +70,16 @@
 	int32_t &exposure = frameContext.sensor.exposure;
 	double &again = frameContext.sensor.gain;
 
-	double error = kExposureOptimal - exposureMSV;
+	/*
+	 * The histogram is taken on raw data, but the AWB gains (all >= 1.0, see
+	 * awb.cpp) brighten the image afterwards by roughly the green gain. Aim
+	 * the raw exposure lower by that factor so the final image lands at the
+	 * optimal level instead of blowing out. With MSV ~ 0.5 + 5 * mean this
+	 * keeps 2.5 for a gain of 1.0.
+	 */
+	const float boost = std::clamp(context.activeState.awb.gains.g(), 1.0f, 4.0f);
+	const double target = 0.5 + (kExposureOptimal - 0.5) / boost;
+	double error = target - exposureMSV;
 
 	if (std::abs(error) <= kExposureSatisfactory)
 		return;
@@ -119,7 +128,7 @@
 	context.activeState.agc.again = again;
 
 	LOG(IPASoftExposure, Debug)
-		<< "exposureMSV " << exposureMSV
+		<< "exposureMSV " << exposureMSV << " target " << target
 		<< " error " << error << " factor " << factor
 		<< " exp " << exposure << " again " << again;
 }
